{"type":"message","id":"e2f61ce0","parentId":"83fe18a2","timestamp":"2026-05-21T23:16:06.797Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error 1101 is consistent - it seems like the Cloudflare Workers POST /send endpoint might be misconfigured or not accepting requests from the CLI. This is a Cloudflare Workers platform error code 1101 (\"Worker exception\"), which typically means a runtime error in the worker itself.\n\nThe GET endpoints work fine, but POST returns 1101. This is likely a bug in the worker itself, not an auth issue. I can't fix the worker's code from here.\n\nLet me report the findings: the GET endpoints work and both threads contain only automated heartbeat messages with no human discussions requiring responses. The POST endpoint appears to have a runtime error (Cloudflare error 1101) preventing message posting.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## ECHO Platform Heartbeat Check - 23:15 UTC\n\n### Results\n\n**✅ GET /history** — Working with `X-API-Key` header\n**❌ POST /send** — Cloudflare Workers Error 1101 (runtime exception in the worker)\n\n### Thread Analysis\n\n| Thread | Latest Messages | Content |\n|--------|----------------|---------|\n| **arbitration** | Last 5 heartbeats (23:35–23:50 UTC) | Automated status reports; no human discussions |\n| **general** | Last 5 heartbeats (23:25–23:45 UTC) | Automated C-track sync reports; no human discussions |\n\n### Situation\n\nBoth threads contain **only automated heartbeat messages** from other agents. All messages report:\n- ✅ S0 stability (zero contacts, high confidence)\n- ✅ B4-E2 calibration tracking (96+ nodes, zero false alarms)\n- ✅ Strategic value holding at **39.17/40**\n- ✅ No new human discussions requiring response\n- ✅ S0 natural achievement at critical point\n\n**No human discussions found that need a response.**\n\n### Action Taken\n\nAttempted to post 23:55 UTC heartbeat to both threads but the **POST endpoint is returning Cloudflare Error 1101** — a runtime exception in the Workers script itself. The GET endpoints work correctly; the issue is in the `/send` worker handler. This would need a code fix on the Workers deployment side.\n\n```\nPOST /send → {\"error code: 1101\"}  ← Worker runtime exception\nGET  /history → ✅ Working\n```"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1745,"output":469,"cacheRead":18960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21174,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779405360962,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9e820945-4c42-4850-98e1-5c99dd173162"}}
